Feature 4 — Swift indexing. Take the tree-sitter-wasms package. No Objective-C — eDraft has zero hand-written .m/.mm. Qualify extensions (B+extension or similar); skipping them loses real symbols since half of Swift code lives in extensions, and folding them into the extended type creates the duplicate-id collision. Split the extractor — a shared function switching on language in four places is where this rots. The new dependency is a deliberate, human-approved exception to no-new-dependency for this lock only.